On Mon, Jan 19, 2004 at 07:51:26PM +0100, Bernd Walter wrote:
> On Tue, Jan 20, 2004 at 03:34:58AM +0900, Ki-Yeol Park wrote:
> > I'm trying to run  FreeBSD 5.2R on an old DEC Alphaserver 1200 system.
> > 
> > 1. Can I use rl(4) ethernet device on this system, though it is not 
> > recognized  by SRM Console?
> 
> The rl driver should work on alpha, although rl based cards are the
> least efficient cards supported by FreeBSD.
> 
> > 2. Is there ANY  recommended ATA or ATA-RAID Controller I can use on 
> > this system?
> 
> Principaly all controllers should work that also work under i386, but
> none is supported by SRM so you need a different media to boot from.

I should add that you must be aware of raid controllers that require
any x86 specific tools/BIOS for setup.

