> replacing the disk, I decided to give 5.2 a go, thinking maybe some of 
> the problems of last year may have been resolved.
> 
> No such luck.
> 
> As you can see below, it's doing the machine check at almost the same 
> point as last year. In combing the archives, it seems that there were 
> problems with some cards, so I yanked out all the pci cards (there were 
> no EISA cards), still a machine check.
> 
> This machine booted and ran stable under 4-xx with a uniprocessor kernel
> 
> It seems you may have to disable the machine checks in order to get this 
> beast to boot, any pointers on where to start?
> I'd like to play with it with FBSD before going back to VMS.
