Well, I built a 2100A kernel without the EISA support and no joy, them machine 
still panics at the probe, this time at the the second pcibus.

The 4.x kernels that booted were all uniprocessor. In 5.x the default generic 
kernels had SMP support enabled and all panicked. I have NOT disabled SMP in 
the kernel config, but, as you asked, set the SRM console to only enable 1 
cpu. If I remember I think I did try a uniprocessor kernel in 5.0 and I 
beleive it panicked also, so it might not be the SMP code, although as you 
said earlier, SMP was not enabled in the 4.x series on Alpha's

Cheers

Tom Ponsford

